<title>CANADA: Independents cheer, majors hit Quebec gasoline plan.</title>
<headline>Independents cheer, majors hit Quebec gasoline plan.</headline>
<byline>Jeffrey Jones</byline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Quebec government's plans announced Thursday to regulate prices in Canada's second-largest gasoline market was met -- not surprisingly -- with cheers from independent retailers and criticism from the major oil companies.</p>
<p>Quebec's independents had called for legislation to end price wars they said were aimed at squeezing them out of the market.</p>
